<h2>STRATOS Voice support</h2>
<p>STRATOS Voice records meetings and transcribes them locally on iPhone. The basic flow is <strong>Record → Transcribe → Read or share</strong>. You can optionally refine text with personal or organisational AI.</p>
<h2>Connecting AI</h2>
<p>In the meeting library, open the menu → <strong>AI review</strong>. Select <strong>Personal AI</strong>, a provider, a model available in your account and your API key. For an enterprise server, also enter its address and supported interface type. The key stays on your iPhone. The provider bills API usage; a chat subscription may not include API access.</p>
<p>For organisational sign-in, choose <strong>STRATOS / AKB → Configure STRATOS</strong>. Your administrator supplies the connection name, HTTPS server address and sign-in address. These may be configured automatically on managed iPhones. Changing the server signs you out but preserves local recordings and transcripts. Do not use a direct database address or an AI provider’s API key as the server address.</p>
<h2>Finding corrected text</h2>
<p>After AI review, you see an <strong>AI-proposed version</strong>. Accepting it creates a new revision, shown in the reader as <strong>Transcript with AI corrections</strong>. Original versions remain in history. Interface labels may be localised.</p>
<h2>Background recording</h2>
<p>Recording does not require internet and may continue in the background. iOS indicates microphone use. A phone call or another activity with exclusive microphone access may interrupt recording. The app preserves completed parts, displays the interruption and attempts to resume when iOS allows it. Before an important meeting, check storage space, battery and the microphone.</p>
<h2>When AI review is unavailable</h2>
<p>Local records and transcripts remain available. Check the internet connection, selected model and API key or STRATOS sign-in. Direct review runs while the app is open. Completed parts survive interruption and you choose whether to continue; the provider may have charged for the last unfinished request. Contact your administrator if organisational restrictions apply. Sending or retrying a review does not happen automatically.</p>
<h2>Contact support</h2>
<p>Support is provided by <strong>VCode</strong>, contact: <strong>podpora@zeleznalady.cz</strong>. Include the app version from <strong>Privacy and information</strong>, iPhone model, iOS version and a short description of the steps. You can explicitly share operational diagnostics from <strong>App status</strong>. Do not send passwords, tokens, work recordings or transcripts without a separate agreement with support and your organisation’s permission.</p>
</Fragment>}
